NAME
       chgrp - change the group of files

SYNOPSIS
       chgrp [OPTION...] GROUP FILE...
       chgrp [OPTION...] --reference=RFILE FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       chgrp sets the group that owns each FILE. GROUP can be a name or a
       number. root may use any group; a file's owner may choose only a group
       they are a member of.

       chgrp GROUP FILE does the same as chown :GROUP FILE.

OPTIONS
       -R, --recursive
              Change the files and directories inside each directory too.

       -v, --verbose
              Report every file processed.

       -c, --changes
              Report only the files that really changed.

       -f, --silent, --quiet
              Do not print most error messages.

       -h, --no-dereference
              Change a symbolic link itself, not the file it points to.

       --reference=RFILE
              Use RFILE's group.

EXAMPLES
       Make devs the group of a shared directory, then add set-group-ID so
       new files get the same group:

           chgrp devs /shared/devs
           chmod g+s /shared/devs

       Change the group of a whole tree:

           chgrp -R wheel /srv/admin

SEE ALSO
       chown(1), chmod(1), groups(1), newgrp(1)
